        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Conus",
        "margin_note": "Name all three arches. Each name is worth part of this mark.",
        "lines": [
          "The ventricle opens into the conus arteriosus",
          "on the VENTRAL side of the heart.",
          "The conus arteriosus is also called the truncus",
          "arteriosus.",
          "It divides into a right and a left trunk.",
          "Each trunk gives rise to three aortic arches:",
          "the carotid arch, the systemic arch and the",
          "pulmocutaneous arch.",
          "Blood leaves the heart through these arches."
        ],
        "why": "The conus arteriosus is the single outlet of the one ventricle, and the three arches are how one stream of blood is shared between the head, the body and the lungs and skin.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that the conus arteriosus leaves the auricle. It leaves the VENTRICLE.",
          "Naming two arches. There are THREE on each side: carotid, systemic and pulmocutaneous."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Three arches, three destinations: carotid to the head, systemic to the body, pulmocutaneous to lungs and skin."
