          "The left auricle receives oxygenated blood from",
          "the lungs.",
          "Both auricles empty into the single ventricle,",
          "so the two kinds of blood mix to some extent.",
          "The circulation of the frog is therefore called",
          "incomplete double circulation."
        ],
        "why": "The single ventricle is the reason for the name: the blood passes through the heart twice in one round, which makes it double, but it is not kept fully apart, which makes it incomplete.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that frog blood does not mix at all. The single ventricle allows some mixing.",
          "Calling it single circulation. Fishes have single circulation; the frog has incomplete DOUBLE circulation."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Double because the blood crosses the heart twice; incomplete because one ventricle cannot keep it apart."
      }
